## Selection Sort

### Approach
- Divide the array into sorted and unsorted parts.
- For every index `i`, find the smallest element in the unsorted portion.
- Swap that smallest element with the element at index `i`.
- Repeat until the entire array is sorted.

### Complexity
- Time Complexity: O(n²)
- Space Complexity: O(1)

SOLUTION :
static int[] SelectionSort(int[] arr, int n) {
        for (int i = 0; i <= n - 1; i++) {
            int min = i;
            for (int j = i; j <= n - 1; j++) {
                if (arr[j] < arr[min]) {
                    min = j;
                }
            }
            int temp = arr[min];
            arr[min] = arr[i];
            arr[i] = temp;
        }
        return arr;
    }
